    {
      "category": "legacy_model_level_reach_inconsistency",
      "finding": "All six base fixture cases initialize an on-scene ground assignment targeting the incident from a staging point outside the declared three-cell useful-work reach. This is a model-level reach inconsistency, not proof of unreachable runtime or physical hazard.",
      "follow_up": "Retain base cases as preliminary regression probes and exclude them from representative handover or training claims. Existing shift and egress constructors require useful staging and a return route or disclose recovery fallback; use supported shift, coverage and current real-map variants within their declared scope. All 32 are development cases."
    },
    {
      "category": "structural_warnings_with_existing_disposition",
      "finding": "28 expansion variants in 14 groups have wind shift at or before ignition; four variants in two groups have population/refuge burning at ignition. These are not automatically infeasible.",
      "existing_disposition": {
        "source": "data/incident_day_v2/README.md",
